// A check that doesn't hold in a function the test called has the calls that led to it
// under its line, innermost first, up to the test fn; one in the test fn itself has none.
// A test's panic has its path, which ends at the test fn too.
//# $ ctxc test {dir}/t
//# exit: 1
//# stdout:
//| {dir}/t/t.ctx:16: fail: in_the_test: 1 + 1 == 3: 2 == 3
//| {dir}/t/t.ctx:3: fail: in_helpers: a == b: 3 == 2
//|   called from helpers::all_twos ({dir}/t/t.ctx:7:27)
//|   called from in_helpers ({dir}/t/t.ctx:21:22)
//| {dir}/t/t.ctx:8: fail: in_helpers: required: xs.len > 5: 2 > 5
//|   called from in_helpers ({dir}/t/t.ctx:21:22)
//| {dir}/t/t.ctx:11:46: fail: panics: panic: index 2 out of bounds for length 2
//|   at helpers::third ({dir}/t/t.ctx:11:46)
//|   at panics ({dir}/t/t.ctx:26:31)
//| tests: 3 run, 0 passed, 3 failed, 0 skipped, 0 not selected, 4 checks

// As JSON, a check's failure has them as `called_from`, and a panic's as `path`.
